$q = 'P674 (the Siege of Sosaria map in the player package): parts 1 to 4 and 6 are done and tested. The package now ships Zigholtul''s map (download 37 MB bigger, 189 MB zip); the first start builds the Trammel and Felucca copies in about 5 seconds (221 MB on disk), later starts skip it, and gate 4 holds the zip to the map''s hashes. Part 5, the version floor, needs your rule: today nothing tells the server which package a client runs, so the fix is a client patch (0009) that sends the package version at login, plus a server check. Staff also log in with other clients (ClassicUO admin, Razor, stock TazUO) that would send no version at all. Which rule do you want? (Part 7, the TazUO pictures on S2''s server, waits for S2, which nobody has started yet; I will do it once S2 exists.)'
& 'D:\UO\golem\Ask-Chase.ps1' -Question $q `
    -Choice 'Refuse old packages, let silent clients in (recommended)|Client patch 0009 sends the package version; the server refuses a package older than the swap with a plain message; a client that sends nothing (staff ClassicUO, Razor, stock TazUO) gets in with one warning line.' `
    -Choice2 'Refuse old and silent clients, staff exempt|Same patch and check, but a client that sends no version is refused too, except on staff accounts.' `
    -Choice3 'Launcher only, no server check|version.json gets a minimum version and Play.ps1 refuses to start an older package and says to update. No client patch and no server change; a player who skips the launcher is not stopped.' `
    -Choice4 'Leave it for later|Mark P674 done without part 5; the version floor goes into S2 or a prompt of its own.'
